 "method_ledger_development": [
  "D4 group generator bug: used transposition (0 3) (fixes ADJACENT square vertices -> closure = S4, |G|=24) instead of diagonal reflection (1 3); CAUGHT by the pre-stated hand-derived law constants (code gave S4's H=2.094361 vs hand D4 1.905639).",
  "F20 generator bug: closure of two translations is C5, not AGL(1,5); CAUGHT by the |G|=20 assert.",
  "Polynomial '1' initialized as np.ones_like -> the poly 1+x+...+x^n; every x^p mod f wrong and ALL type histograms collapsed (H~0.006); CAUGHT by the sympy factor_list ground-truth gate (150 primes/field) and brute-force root counts.",
  "Square-and-multiply scanned exponent bits LSB-first under the MSB-first Horner recurrence E<-2E+b: computed x^(2^22+revbits(p)) mod f, not x^p; types still collapsed after fix 3; CAUGHT by single-prime sympy comparison of x^p mod f.",
  "Ramified-prime test first written as q^2 | disc (would have missed ramified odd primes with squarefree disc, e.g. p=31 for x^3+x+1); corrected to prime-divides-disc via sympy.factorint(disc) before any measurement.",
  "abelian_table asserted distinct type LABELS == nquot; false in general (distinct cosets can share a cycle type, e.g. C3@7 cosets {2,5},{3,4} both [3]); assertion corrected to count distinct COSETS.",
  "Design misregistration corrected BEFORE the full run and disclosed in header: (a) permutation-null z is a dependence-significance statistic (expected huge for every field since the null destroys real Chebotarev dependence), NOT a law-deviation statistic; (b) null-mean subtraction over-corrects structured joint tables (shuffles occupy more cells), so I_meas = Miller-Madow-corrected plug-in MI, with raw and null reported alongside."
 ]
